Architectural notes / limitations
•	The implemented MCP transport is HTTP/JSON and minimal. If you require a specific MCP SDK or protocol format (e.g., a precise Model Context Protocol wire format used by a specific LLM runtime), we can adapt the discovery/invoke payloads to that spec. For now, this implementation provides standard discovery + invocation endpoints compatible with most tool-calling runtimes and documents tool schemas.
•	Authentication relies on NB_SID cookie being presented by the MCP caller. If the LLM runtime cannot send cookies, integrate a server-side mediator that authenticates users and calls these MCP endpoints on their behalf; do not accept CustomerId from the LLM.
